impl.summary:
The Cloudflare Worker in /home/user/code/worker is implemented per SPEC.md: Ed25519 request auth, crews and invites, clip registry, quota-checked presigned R2 PUT/GET URLs (aws4fetch, 900 s), clip deletion, and an hourly cron sweep. I also wrote migrations/0001_init.sql, wrangler.toml and a Portuguese README.md (setup, lifecycle backstop, API reference). Both required checks pass, and a local run under `wrangler dev` (workerd with simulated D1 and R2) also worked. Presigned URLs were never tried against real R2, since there are no credentials here.

Tests: the D1 tests run the real SQL from src/db.ts on in-memory SQLite (`node:sqlite`) loaded with the real migration. R2, the clock and the RNG are in-memory and seeded. The suite is 231 tests in about 2.3 s, with no network. I broke eight things on purpose (quota limits, replay window, invite uses, membership, pov check, skew check, retry accounting) and the tests caught each one.

The local `wrangler dev` smoke test covered:
- device registration, crew, invite and join;
- clip registration, upload and download URLs, replay rejection;
- DELETE removing exactly one clip's objects from the simulated R2;
- the cron sweep.

Presigned URLs match an independent SigV4 computation in the tests.

review.checks:
All required checks pass. cargo fmt -p duoclip-clock (then --check: OK). cargo clippy -p duoclip-clock --all-targets -- -D warnings: clean. cargo test -p duoclip-clock: 61 unit (1 ignored real-network test), 20 new adversarial, 11 simulation and 1 doctest passed, about 1 s of test time. cargo check -p duoclip-clock --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu (also --all-targets): OK. RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings cargo doc --no-deps: OK. No new dependencies.

Checked mathematically, no defect found:
- offset/delay formulas and sign conventions, for both server and peer (also tested end to end in sign_conventions_server_and_peer);
- ppb units, and the WLS weights (a scaled but equivalent form);
- feasible slope range: it is the exact projection (Fourier-Motzkin);
- LP worst case: the duality basis argument holds;
- Marzullo: brute force over 3000 random cases with touching endpoints and ties;
- fixed-point monotonicity: floor(a+b) >= floor(a)+floor(b) with q > -2^48, plus exact continuity at every cut;
- slew clamp and duration; step rules (exact threshold boundaries); holdover growth; local_at as the inverse of utc_at across 300 segments;
- NTP: era pivot around 2036 and at extreme pivots; rejection order (cookie before KoD before LI=3);
- scheduler: 15 s minimum interval and 1024 s caps (property test over 200 seeds).

Mutation testing on a scratch copy: all 11 mutants are killed. Wrong rate sign in offset_at kills 15 tests, including the 99% honesty and pipeline tests. Wrong offset sign kills 19. Halved bound kills the honesty tests. Dropping delay/2 from the hard bound kills 12. Negated WLS slope kills the rate convergence test. Disabling falseticker rejection, using one-sided remap and removing holdover growth are all caught. Five of the new adversarial tests fail on the original code: two for the late update, one each for aging, the contradicted rate and the slack.
